A||||2||DISenchanted||Wheel Bearings.||||1
Z||000000||DISenchanted||09-30-1999||12:00 AM||||I must be one of the dumbest people alive.  My wheelbearing went out on me so I decided I'd replace it.  I couldn't find my hayes mannual, so I just did what made sense.  Now I'm at an Impass.  I can't get the little aluminum cover plate to go back on.  I think I bent it.  I need a new one and I need to know how I should put it back on.  Any Idea's?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||09-30-1999||12:31 AM||||What aluminum cover plate? If you mean the seal on the back side for the inner bearings, you need to buy new ones, don't try to reuse the seals. If you mean the outer steel dust cover hub thingie that covers the cotter pin and nut, carefully tap it into place with a small hammer. Hopefully you packed the bearings real good with grease and used a torque wrench to properly tighten them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||09-30-1999||12:34 AM||||I'm assuming it's the front,had one once that kept popping back off every time I tried to pound it on with a mallet.<BR>Finally put a very large socket over it and pounded very hard.||||reg||11
